From 37d27fd25c6a27302fc8491828c8c70c1a452f0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:43:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 98/99] icon_manager: Adopts layer surfaces as dock-apps
 ("wlmaker-dockapp").

A layer-shell client with the namespace "wlmaker-dockapp" (eg. a system
tray written with GTK and gtk-layer-shell) becomes a dock-app: Its
surface is the content of a tile, placed and handled as the dock-apps of
the icon protocol. It is dragged between the Dock, the Clip and the
drawers, removed with the kaboom, has the dock-app's menu, and goes with
the dock's level. Layer, anchor and margins are ignored; the surface
keeps the size it asked for, up to the tile's.

The right button goes to the surface where it takes input (its input
region, eg. the tray's icons), else it opens the tile's menu; the balloon
is not shown there either. Elsewhere on the tile (its border, or outside
the input region), the left button drags the tile. Popups of the surface
(menus, balloons) are placed in an empty dock in the overlay layer, at
the surface's origin: Above all.

The balloon's command of a script leaves out the interpreter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
